archived

# Fuzzing. The corpus and the artifacts are generated - ten megabytes across a few thousand
# files after a minute of fuzzing - and none of it is worth reviewing in a diff. What *is*
# committed is `fuzz/seeds`, which is hand-written and small: the shapes a fuzzer would take a
# long time to reach on its own, including the one that used to abort the process.
/fuzz/target
/fuzz/corpus
/fuzz/artifacts

# Generated by deploy/cluster/tokens.sh. A credential that reaches a repository is not a
# credential.
deploy/cluster/secrets
deploy/single/secrets

# `make start`: the local database, its log and its pid. A playground, not a fixture.
/.local

# Kept local: the gap list is worked on outside the repository.
checklist.md
big-web
/target-base
